---
source: tests/attestation_state.rs
description: "The attestation state that lives on the localnet once e2e/run.sh has run. For each subject: the attestations at its active box and at its revoked address, both derived off-chain from the registry and subject ids, with their data and rendered Display; then every registry event, in order. Ids are replaced with names: a package's directory name, `name@vN` for version N of an upgraded package, or a label from the test. A line starting with `!!` marks an inconsistency."
---
